{
  "linkedin": "Winter tramping means preparing for changing conditions on the trail. A proper layering system helps you stay comfortable as you move through the backcountry. Start with a moisture-managing base layer like our Merino 200, priced at $119, followed by a fleece or puffer mid layer such as the Ridge fleece for $139, and finish with a weather-resistant shell. Avoid cotton since it retains moisture. Adjust your clothing levels before you start to sweat to maintain a steady temperature throughout your hike. Read more on our blog: https://acmeoutdoorgear.example.com/blog/layering-101 #NewZealand #Tramping #OutdoorGear",
  "instagram": "Staying comfortable on winter tramping trips comes down to the right combination of layers. Keep sweat away with a merino or synthetic base, trap your body heat with a fleece or puffer mid layer, and block wind and rain with a shell. Steer clear of cotton, as it stays wet. Try our Merino 200 base layer for $119 and the Ridge fleece for $139. Remember to adjust your layers before you get too warm on the trail. Link in bio. #AcmeOutdoorGear #WinterTramping #NewZealandOutdoors #Bushcraft #HikingNZ",
